Mi Pad 2 RT5659 UCM profile; devices: Speaker, Headphones, IntMic, HeadsetMic.

The bypass paths support both the 6.14 unprefixed Amp Input/Amp Input1 controls
and the 7.2 codec_conf-prefixed Left Amp Input/Right Amp Input controls. A complete
prefixed pair is preferred when both layouts exist. Partial/unknown layouts
are rejected before mixer writes. Both channels are selected before speaker
power is enabled. This keeps one UCM configuration across kernel rollback.

pkgrel9 adds the optional 7.2 factory DSP backend. It requires the left and
right Profile controls with their corresponding musicL/musicR enum strings and
both Stop controls. Partial or mixed factory/bypass controls fail before any
mixer write. Speaker enable powers the speaker path off, applies the two named
profiles, disables headphones and then enables the speaker path. Headphone and
capture sequences do not select factory profiles.

The existing RT5659 DAC1 mixer supplies speaker volume. The factory music
profiles have one vstep, so UCM neither models the two TFA Master Volume
controls as volume sliders nor writes them. It never writes Stop: the kernel's
C2C/DAPM path must own amplifier start/stop along with clocks. UCM does not
enable a deferred factory DSP and does not calibrate hardware.

Real libasound 1.2.15.3/1.2.16.1 parsing and synthetic-control sequence tests:
  python3 fix_file/tests/mipad2-ucm-real-parser-test.py
Requires GCC and ALSA development files; --alsa-root and --libdir accept an
isolated root and library path relative to it.
These tests are not physical audio, DAPM, jack IRQ or acoustic validation.
